cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use pyplotrs in work you publish, please cite it."
title: pyplotrs
abstract: >-
  A publication-quality plotting library for Python with a Rust rendering core.
  Produces PDF whose text stays embedded, selectable and editable rather than
  outlined, alongside SVG, PNG and self-contained HTML.
type: software
authors:
  - alias: tkclam
    email: thomas.lam@epfl.ch
repository-code: "https://github.com/tkclam/pyplotrs"
url: "https://tkclam.github.io/pyplotrs/"
license: MIT
# Bump both alongside `[workspace.package].version` in Cargo.toml when cutting a
# release; GitHub's "Cite this repository" widget reads them verbatim.
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-08-20"
keywords:
  - plotting
  - visualization
  - scientific-visualization
  - publication-figures
  - rust
  - python
